## qf-mind3 | Quick-fire: learning | psych | 0 | - | qf-psy2
quiz 3 | Which study method works best for long-term retention?
* Spaced self-testing
o Re-reading
o Highlighting
o Cramming the night before
= Testing plus spacing beat passive review in study after study.
> Next

quiz 3 | Explaining a concept in simple words to find gaps is called…
* The Feynman technique
o The Pomodoro technique
o The method of loci
o Mind mapping
= If you can't explain it simply, you don't understand it yet.
> Next

quiz 3 | The "method of loci" (memory palace) uses…
* Imagined places along a familiar route
o Rhymes
o Flashcards
o Colour coding
= Memory champions use it to memorise card decks in seconds.
> Next

quiz 4 | Why does sleeping after studying help?
* Sleep consolidates memories
o It resets IQ
o It erases distractions
o It doesn't help
= Especially deep sleep and REM.
> Next

quiz 4 | "Desirable difficulties" means…
* Some struggle while learning improves long-term retention
o Hard exams are always better
o Learning should be painful
o Difficult teachers are best
= Spacing, interleaving and testing feel harder but work better.
> Next

quiz 4 | Interleaving means…
* Mixing different problem types in one session
o Studying one topic until mastered
o Studying with friends
o Taking breaks
= It trains you to pick the right method.
