## qf-life | Quick-fire: life science 3 | bio | 0 | - | qf-bio2
quiz 3 | What does DNA stand for?
* Deoxyribonucleic acid
o Dinitrogen acid
o Deoxyribose nitrogen acid
o Double nucleic acid
= The molecule of heredity.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which animal is closest to humans genetically?
* Chimpanzees (and bonobos)
o Gorillas
o Orangutans
o Dolphins
= We share roughly 98–99% of comparable DNA.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which gas do plants release during photosynthesis?
* Oxygen
o Carbon dioxide
o Nitrogen
o Methane
= Earth's oxygen came from billions of years of photosynthesis.
> Next

quiz 4 | What do bees collect to make honey?
* Nectar
o Pollen
o Sap
o Water
= Pollen is food for larvae.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which is the only mammal capable of true flight?
* Bats
o Flying squirrels
o Sugar gliders
o Colugos
= The others glide.
> Next

quiz 4 | How long does light-sensitive vision adaptation to darkness take to mostly complete?
* About 20–30 minutes
o About 5 seconds
o About 2 hours
o About 1 minute
= Rod cells regenerate their pigment slowly.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which organ filters your blood to make urine?
* The kidneys
o The liver
o The bladder
o The spleen
= About 180 litres of blood plasma filtered per day; most is reabsorbed.
> Next

quiz 4 | What is the main function of red blood cells?
* Carrying oxygen
o Fighting infection
o Clotting
o Digesting food
= They have no nucleus, leaving room for haemoglobin.
